# One line-ending truth on every platform. A Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true otherwise rewrites the whole tree on the way in, which
# turns `zig fmt --check` into a wall of failures and makes the vendored tree
# differ from its upstream pin for a reason that is not a real change.
# Checkout must not be a transform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The vendored tree is compared byte-for-byte against its upstream pin by
# ci/verify-vendor.sh, so git must never transform it at all.
libs/** -text
